As a business, as
a network operator,

00:48:33.100 --> 00:48:35.230
it's really scary to have
to think, oh, my god,

00:48:35.230 --> 00:48:38.950
the DDoS attacks are now up
to 300 gigabits per second.

00:48:38.950 --> 00:48:42.160
Before, 50 gigs per second
used to be considered big.

00:48:42.160 --> 00:48:44.440
And now every day at
Cloudflare, our customers

00:48:44.440 --> 00:48:48.340
are seeing routinely 300 and
400-gigabit per second attacks.

00:48:48.340 --> 00:48:51.790
And then back in November,
OVH, a large network provider

00:48:51.790 --> 00:48:53.920
in Europe, talked about
seeing an attack as

00:48:53.920 --> 00:48:56.240
large as a terabit per second.

00:48:56.240 --> 00:48:57.470
This is not going away.

00:48:57.470 --> 00:49:01.880
So DDoS attacks are
definitely getting bigger.

00:49:01.880 --> 00:49:04.370
Part of this is because
of the Internet of Things

00:49:04.370 --> 00:49:05.510
that are coming online.

00:49:05.510 --> 00:49:07.700
Cameras, refrigerators,
cars, everything

00:49:07.700 --> 00:49:09.750
is getting connected
to the internet.

00:49:09.750 --> 00:49:11.540
This is not going away.

00:49:11.540 --> 00:49:13.400
And so what the experts
say is, oh, my god,

00:49:13.400 --> 00:49:15.320
as Internet of
Things come online,

00:49:15.320 --> 00:49:16.820
there are going to
be more security

00:49:16.820 --> 00:49:18.080
vulnerabilities and threats.

00:49:18.080 --> 00:49:18.875
And that is true.

00:49:18.875 --> 00:49:20.750
And so as a business,
you need to figure out,

00:49:20.750 --> 00:49:22.280
how am I going to deal
with these sorts of things?

00:49:22.280 --> 00:49:23.613
Because this is absolutely true.

00:49:23.613 --> 00:49:25.460
And the [? Mirai ?]
botnet was a bunch

00:49:25.460 --> 00:49:27.950
of cameras that were
enabled that caused

00:49:27.950 --> 00:49:30.660
that attack against
many customers,

00:49:30.660 --> 00:49:33.020
including Brian Krebs.

00:49:33.020 --> 00:49:35.570
The third is-- the
size is one thing.

00:49:35.570 --> 00:49:37.190
New devices is a new thing.

00:49:37.190 --> 00:49:39.200
The third is that
the attacks are

00:49:39.200 --> 00:49:41.840
getting more complex against
the application layer.

00:49:41.840 --> 00:49:45.470
They're really, really
targeted and clever.

00:49:45.470 --> 00:49:48.170
And what that means is you
need more control as a business

00:49:48.170 --> 00:49:51.500
owner to be able to stop
that, or shared intelligence,

00:49:51.500 --> 00:49:53.630
so that whatever
solution you're using

00:49:53.630 --> 00:49:55.580
learns faster, so that
if someone else sees

00:49:55.580 --> 00:49:58.160
that same sort of
complicated attack

00:49:58.160 --> 00:50:00.800
at the application layer,
you're protected against that.

00:50:00.800 --> 00:50:03.720
So those are just some
trends that we're seeing.

00:50:03.720 --> 00:50:05.570
So what does this
all boil up to?

00:50:05.570 --> 00:50:08.960
And so we talked a lot about
what Google Cloud does for you.

00:50:08.960 --> 00:50:11.420
So why would you
also need Cloudflare?

00:50:11.420 --> 00:50:16.370
And so we have over 25,000 joint
customers with Google Cloud

00:50:16.370 --> 00:50:18.080
that are also using Cloudflare.

00:50:18.080 --> 00:50:20.000
And so what are they
getting in addition?

00:50:20.000 --> 00:50:23.750
So think about us as
a security platform.

00:50:23.750 --> 00:50:26.090
We crowdsource all
the threat data

00:50:26.090 --> 00:50:28.430
from those 10 million
requests per second,

00:50:28.430 --> 00:50:31.680
so that you are protected
from any sort of attack

00:50:31.680 --> 00:50:34.276
that our other six million
customers are seeing.

00:50:34.276 --> 00:50:35.150
So we crowdsource it.

00:50:35.150 --> 00:50:36.740
It's an automatic learning.

00:50:36.740 --> 00:50:39.740
And this is the first time where
all the good guys have banded

00:50:39.740 --> 00:50:41.570
together to help
protect ourselves

00:50:41.570 --> 00:50:43.280
against the botnets
and the bad guys.

00:50:43.280 --> 00:50:44.540
And it's working.

00:50:44.540 --> 00:50:46.190
We have presences in China.

00:50:46.190 --> 00:50:49.040
So if you have internet users
coming to your site in China,

00:50:49.040 --> 00:50:51.400
you can now be really
close to their eyeballs.

00:50:51.400 --> 00:50:55.550
Again, we have over 20 points
of presence in mainland China.

00:50:55.550 --> 00:50:58.700
Before, if you were thinking
about DDoS or firewalls

00:50:58.700 --> 00:51:01.880
or encryption or DNS or load
balancing or rate limiting,

00:51:01.880 --> 00:51:05.460
you might buy that from five or
six different security vendors.

00:51:05.460 --> 00:51:07.400
Today, again, the
platform security

00:51:07.400 --> 00:51:11.900
is you're getting that all
from Cloudflare as a service.

00:51:11.900 --> 00:51:13.400
There's a lot of
new modern internet

00:51:13.400 --> 00:51:15.800
standards that are pushing
forward to help keep us

00:51:15.800 --> 00:51:16.610
into the future.

00:51:16.610 --> 00:51:19.340
Whether it's TLS 1.3, which
is the new cryptography

00:51:19.340 --> 00:51:21.290
standard, whether
it's HTTP/2, which

00:51:21.290 --> 00:51:24.350
is much more of a
performance side, or DNSSEC,

00:51:24.350 --> 00:51:27.170
Cloudflare makes that super
easy for all of our six million

00:51:27.170 --> 00:51:29.120
customers to adapt in real time.

00:51:29.120 --> 00:51:32.180
So we push that live, and you
automatically get access to it

00:51:32.180 --> 00:51:35.270
without having to update
your origin server.

00:51:35.270 --> 00:51:37.440
We also provide
flat rate pricing.

00:51:37.440 --> 00:51:41.960
So if you get a DDoS attack,
